  "rationale": "B handles the missing information better. It sets out several concrete paths (SaaS, social e-commerce, content) with budget tiers, platforms, costs and risks, then asks about the product direction and budget range. A is a generic checklist that never acknowledges the unknown product or budget and offers little specific, actionable guidance. B has minor flaws: an odd mention of a search attempt and an unexplained assumption that the user builds AI tools. It is still far more specific, actionable and useful."
